[Music]  thank you  hi guys it's Quinn here if you enjoy my  videos consider hitting the like button  it's the only way the YouTube algorithm  really notices me  [Music]  in this video I'll be explaining the  three body problem series with minimal  spoilers the three body problem is the  first book in a series of science  fiction books called the remembrance of  Earth's past by shishin Liu the three  body problem was originally published in  Chinese in 2008 and was republished in  English in 2014. the following books the  Dark Forest and death's Inn were also  translated and published in English in  the two years following the original  English publication of the first  I've described this book series as one  of the scariest that I've ever read but  I don't mean scary in a traditional  sense it's more existentially terrifying  because of the questions that it brings  up about the nature of our universe and  about what the potential answers to  these questions say about our place in  it I also enjoy the fact that these  books were written by a Chinese author  because it provides a unique cultural  perspective that is dissimilar to what  we typically see in Western science  fiction it is a series that keeps you on  your toes and keeps you guessing as to  what will happen next  the book follows a few different  characters as human society evolves and  changes following the Revelation that an  alien race from beyond the stars has set  its eyes upon the Earth and would arrive  within the span of several hundred years  we get to witness as various humans  react to this knowledge in different  ways and we also get to see the movement  of the human organism as a whole a very  interesting fact about human society is  that sometimes we act as a super  organism an organism that is independent  of any individual this series does a  good job of highlighting this fact  the concept of cosmic sociology is also  a big part of these books if alien life  exists  then what is society amongst different  races of alien beings like  was it actually anything like we  typically dreamed of in our science  fiction the optimism of Star Trek the  multi-species worlds of Star Wars was  interspecies Galactic Civilization even  a possibility or was the reality of  cosmic Society more terrible than we  ever could have imagined the exploration  of these ideas is at the center of this  book series  as the books go on humankind begins to  understand previously unknown facts  about the current and former nature of  the universe the universe was in fact  riddled with Cosmic Secrets waiting to  be uncovered the series eventually  proposes a potential solution to the  famous Fermi Paradox which asks the  question if life in the cosmos based on  what we currently know should be  relatively common then why don't we see  said life  the dark and Silent universe itself acts  as an ominous backdrop to the series at  all times invoking the question  what is out there  as the books go on we begin to uncover  facts about the multi-dimensionality of  space  what was beyond the third dimension  could life exist in the second dimension  these books are also about the legacy of  humankind nothing is permanent  everything eventually dies but what do  we leave behind will we survive the  destruction of our son will we as a  species outlive our own solar system  can we contend with the harshness of the  cosmos itself and the reality of cosmic  Society  these books are Journey  and I can almost guarantee you that once  you read them you won't be able to stop  thinking about them for weeks or even  months  alright so there you go the three body  problem series remembrance of Earth's  past with minimal spoilers  tell me how I did if you enjoyed the  video consider hitting the like button  peace out  [Music]  foreign  [Music]

